Package: FTIR.LDIR.Raman
Title: Multi-Instrument Microplastic Particle Matching Pipeline
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kristof", "Moeller",
           email = "kristof-moeller@t-online.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ingests particle data and images from three microspectroscopy
    instruments (FTIR, Raman, LDIR), aligns their spatial coordinate systems
    with a landmark + RANSAC + ICP + thin-plate-spline pipeline, matches
    particles across instrument pairs, scores inter-instrument material
    agreement, and serves an interactive Shiny viewer of the matched dataset.
    This DESCRIPTION exists to declare the dependency surface for reproducible
    environments (renv); the project is run by sourcing main.R rather than
    installed as a package.
License: Proprietary — not yet licensed for public distribution (see README).
    A public license must be chosen before Zenodo / journal deposit.
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    clue,
    dplyr,
    ggplot2,
    ggrepel,
    jpeg,
    jsonlite,
    magick,
    png,
    RANN,
    readxl,
    rintrojs,
    shiny
Suggests:
    reticulate
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.8) with numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib
    (optional — enables the preferred LDIR image backend; the pipeline falls
    back to an R-based segmentation when Python or reticulate is unavailable).
